      "topic": {
        "text": "Variable scope in loops",
        "refs": ["Q0001"]
      },
      "explanation_text": {
        "text": "When a variable is declared inside a block (e.g., inside a while loop), its scope is limited to that block and it cannot be accessed outside of it, which leads to a compilation error such as \"cannot resolve symbol\".",
        "refs": ["Q0001"]
      },
      "explanation_type": null
    },
    {
      "topic": {
        "text": "Compilation error caused by out‑of‑scope variable",
        "refs": ["Q0000"]
      },
      "explanation_text": {
        "text": "If a variable (e.g., principal) is used outside the block where it was declared, the compiler reports an error \"cannot resolve symbol principal\" because the name is not in scope at that point.",
        "refs": ["Q0000"]
      },
      "explanation_type": null
    }
  ],
  "examples": [],
  "facts": [
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "A variable declared inside a while loop is scoped only to that loop block.",
        "refs": ["Q0001"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "Declaring a variable outside the loop and initializing it (e.g., int principal = 0;) resolves the \"cannot resolve symbol\" compilation error.",
        "refs": ["Q0001", "Q0002"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "If user input for annual interest is not between 1 and 30, an error message should be printed and the loop should continue.",
        "refs": ["Q0002"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "Monthly interest must be declared outside its calculation block to avoid a compilation error.",
        "refs": ["Q0003"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "Number of years must be validated (1 ≤ years ≤ 30) before calculating number of payments.",
        "refs": ["Q0004"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    }
  ],
  "formulas": [],
  "procedures": [
    {
      "procedure_name": {
        "text": "Fix variable‑scope compilation errors in mortgage calculator",
        "refs": ["Q0001", "Q0003", "Q0004"]
      },
      "steps": [
        {
          "text": "Identify variables declared inside loops (e.g., principal, monthly interest).",
          "refs": ["Q0000", "Q0001", "Q0003"]
        },
        {
          "text": "Move each variable declaration to a position before the loop so it is in the outer block.",
          "refs": ["Q0001", "Q0003"]
        },
        {
          "text": "Initialize the moved variables (e.g., int principal = 0; float monthlyInterest = 0;).",
          "refs": ["Q0001", "Q0002"]
        },
        {
          "text": "Remove the original declarations from inside the loops.",
          "refs": ["Q0001", "Q0003"]
        },
        {
          "text": "Add input validation inside the loop: if the entered value is outside the allowed range, print an error message (e.g., \"Enter a value between 1 and 30\") and continue looping; otherwise, perform calculations and break out of the loop.",
          "refs": ["Q0002", "Q0003", "Q0004"]
        },
        {
          "text": "Compile and verify that the \"cannot resolve symbol\" errors are gone.",
          "refs": ["Q0000", "Q0001", "Q0003"]
        }
      ],
      "prerequisites": null,
      "outcomes": null,
      "content": {
        "text": "Procedure to correct scope‑related compilation errors in a mortgage‑calculation program.",
        "refs": ["Q0001", "Q0003", "Q0004"]
      }
    }
  ],
